    title="Employment law for employers"
    description="Advice for small employers in Ostrey County: handbooks, classification, offer letters, discipline, terminations and responding to claims."
    lines={['Employment law,', '*for employers.*']}
>
    <p>Employment law is the part of the law a small business meets most often and plans for least. Hiring, paying, scheduling, disciplining and letting people go are governed by a thicket of federal and state rules, and most of the trouble we see began with a decision made quickly by a good manager who did not know one of them.</p>
    <p>Our employment practice advises employers, and most of its value is in the call before the decision. A short conversation about a termination, a classification or a policy costs very little; a claim brought because of one costs a great deal, whoever wins.</p>
</PracticePage>
